IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa1-part4-appeals`

-- Tests of oa1-part4-appeals. Every expected value is worked by hand from the text.

§ `s 27: a change of basis of the Consumer Price Index`

#ASSERT `s 27: a corresponding adjustment shall be made in the Consumer Price Index with respect to the adjustment quarter` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27: a corresponding adjustment shall be made in the Consumer Price Index with respect to the adjustment quarter` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27: a corresponding adjustment shall be made in the Consumer Price Index with respect to the adjustment quarter` FALSE TRUE)

§ `s 27.1(1): time for a request`

-- Notified March 1, 2026: ninety days after is May 30, 2026 (March 31 + April 30 + May 29... worked: March 1 + 90 days = May 30).
#ASSERT `s 27.1: the request is made within the time allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 30) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1: the request is made within the time allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 31) NOTHING)
-- A longer period the Minister allows, before or after the ninety days expire.
#ASSERT `s 27.1: the request is made within the time allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 7 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1: the request is made within the time allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 8 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 7 31)))
#ASSERT `s 27.1: the request is made within the time allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15))
-- The request itself: dissatisfied, in time, in the prescribed form and manner.
#ASSERT `s 27.1(1): the person may make a request to the Minister for a reconsideration of the decision or determination` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1(1): the person may make a request to the Minister for a reconsideration of the decision or determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1(1): the person may make a request to the Minister for a reconsideration of the decision or determination` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1(1): the person may make a request to the Minister for a reconsideration of the decision or determination` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `s 27.1(1.1): a penalty`

#ASSERT `s 27.1(1.1): the person may request the Minister to reconsider the decision to impose a penalty or the amount of the penalty` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1(1.1): the person may request the Minister to reconsider the decision to impose a penalty or the amount of the penalty` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1(1.1): the person may request the Minister to reconsider the decision to impose a penalty or the amount of the penalty` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1(1.1): the person may request the Minister to reconsider the decision to impose a penalty or the amount of the penalty` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1(1.1): the person may request the Minister to reconsider the decision to impose a penalty or the amount of the penalty` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `s 27.1(2): decision of the Minister`

#ASSERT `s 27.1(2): the Minister may reach the outcome on reconsideration` `s 27.1(2): Decision confirmed`
#ASSERT `s 27.1(2): the Minister may reach the outcome on reconsideration` `s 27.1(2): Decision varied`
#ASSERT `s 27.1(2): the Minister may reach the outcome on reconsideration` `s 27.1(2): Payment of a benefit approved`
#ASSERT `s 27.1(2): the Minister may reach the outcome on reconsideration` `s 27.1(2): Amount of a benefit determined`
#ASSERT `s 27.1(2): the Minister may reach the outcome on reconsideration` `s 27.1(2): No benefit determined to be payable`
-- Having received a request, the Minister reconsiders, notifies in writing and gives reasons; failing any of the three is a failure to do what is required.
#ASSERT `s 27.1(2): the Minister has done what the Minister is required to do on the request` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1(2): the Minister has done what the Minister is required to do on the request` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1(2): the Minister has done what the Minister is required to do on the request` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27.1(2): the Minister has done what the Minister is required to do on the request` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Nothing is required before a request is received.
#ASSERT `s 27.1(2): the Minister has done what the Minister is required to do on the request` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `s 28(1): appeal`

#ASSERT `s 28(1): the person may appeal the decision to the Social Security Tribunal` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28(1): the person may appeal the decision to the Social Security Tribunal` FALSE)

§ `s 28(2): reference as to income`

#ASSERT `s 28(2): the appeal on that ground must be referred for decision to the Tax Court of Canada` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28(2): the appeal on that ground must be referred for decision to the Tax Court of Canada` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 28(2): the decision of the Tax Court of Canada is final and binding for all purposes of the appeal to the Social Security Tribunal` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28(2): the decision of the Tax Court of Canada is final and binding for all purposes of the appeal to the Social Security Tribunal` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28(2): the decision of the Tax Court of Canada is final and binding for all purposes of the appeal to the Social Security Tribunal` FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 28(3): stay pending judicial review`

-- The period for judicial review expires March 15, 2027; Her Majesty has not applied: the stay runs to March 15, 2027.
#ASSERT `s 28(3): the last day until which the Minister may stay payment of the benefit` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15)
-- Her Majesty applied and the proceedings were completed in June 2027 (to June 30, 2027), which is later.
#ASSERT `s 28(3): the last day until which the Minister may stay payment of the benefit` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 6 10)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 6 30)
-- ... completed in March 2027 (to March 31, 2027), also later than March 15.
#ASSERT `s 28(3): the last day until which the Minister may stay payment of the benefit` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 3 2)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 3 31)
-- ... completed in February 2027 (to February 28, 2027), earlier than March 15: March 15 is later.
#ASSERT `s 28(3): the last day until which the Minister may stay payment of the benefit` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 2 10)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15)
-- No decision of the Tribunal, no stay.
#ASSERT `s 28(3): the last day until which the Minister may stay payment of the benefit` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2027 3 15) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
